    "feesApplyText": "Relevant letting fees and tenant protection information\t\n\nBefore the tenancy starts (payable to Ocean Letting & Management Ltd  the Agent ) \nHolding Deposit: 1 week s rent\nDeposit: 5 weeks  rent. This is worked out by multiplying the rent by 12, dividing that figure by 52 and then multiplying that figure by 5.\nSo for example if the rent was £1,000pcm\n£1,000 multiply by 12 = £12,000\n£12,000 divide by 52 = £230.77\n£230.77 multiply by 5 = £1,153.85\nSo the deposit will be £1,153.85\n\nDuring the tenancy (payable to the Agent) \nAs well as paying the rent, you may also be required to make the following permitted payments.\n\nPermitted payments\nPayment of [up to £300 + VAT] if you want to change the tenancy agreement.\nPayment of interest for the late payment of rent at a rate of 3% above the Bank of England s base rate.\nPayment of the invoice cost for the reasonably incurred costs for the loss of keys/security devices\nPayment of any unpaid rent and other reasonable costs associated with your early termination of the tenancy that the landlord would incur for remarketing\n\nTenant protection\nOcean Letting & Management Ltd is a member of ARLA, which is our Governing body and a client money protection scheme, and also a member of The Property Ombudsman, which is a redress scheme. You can find out more details on the agent s website or by contacting the agent directly\n\nFull details of our landlord fees can be found at  \n",
